  "question": {
    "text": "Water flows m a horizontal tube (see figure). The pressure of water changes by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> between <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> where the area of cross section are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. Find the rate of flow of water through the tube. (density of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> )<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/395a7730-07a2-4438-a9b9-7122560771ee.jpeg\" />",
